Chart: A directory containing a packaged collection of Kubernetes resource blueprints, 
 configuration files, and metadata.

Values (values.yaml): The central variables file. This separates environment-specific 
 configuration from the application architecture.

Templates (templates/): Manifest blueprints written with the Go template 
 engine ({{ .Values.<key> }}) that generate standard Kubernetes YAML at deployment time.

Release: A specific running instance of a chart in your cluster. You can deploy the exact 
 same chart multiple times with different values (e.g., release web-dev and release web-prod).
